{
  "base": "origin/main",
  "claims": [
    "LR3-C1: the labelled set ships with a licence note and a count of gold facts per fact type, and the corpus's own files are unchanged.",
    "LR3-C2: replay of the recorded run makes zero producer calls and reproduces the figures byte for byte.",
    "LR3-C3: the record gives recall and precision per stage with numerator and denominator, and names the producer, budget and roster.",
    "LR3-C4: a changed gold fact, a changed response and a changed section each change the figure or refuse, and the scoring rule tells found from found with the wrong predicate.",
    "The scoring rule in reference_fixture/README.md is exactly what reference_set.score computes, for every legal run folder, not only the recorded one; the schedule derives nothing from the labels.",
    "The page and the issue reply state nothing the run does not show, and do not present the figure as a claim about other corpora or models.",
    "Every regular expression, string split, slice and special-case branch this change adds handles the whole class of input it is given, not only the examples in the tests and fixtures, and none reads structured text that a parser or an existing reader in this repository already reads."
  ],
