  "question": "This diff against main holds phases LR1, LR2 and LR3 of one milestone; LR1 and LR2 were reviewed before. Review LR3: src/gnd/examples/literature/reference_set.py, reference_fixture/ (README, labels, roster, profile, run, run-record.json, score.json), tools/record_lr3_reference_run.py, tests/test_lr3_reference_set.py, the docs/literature/index.md section 'How much does the reading find?', and notes/issue-reply.md. Does the reference set measure what its README and the page say it measures, are the figures what the scorer computes from the recorded run, and can each test fail when the behaviour it names is wrong?",
